SYNTHESIS_RULES = '\nLEARNING-FOCUSED SYNTHESIS\nExplain each distinct relationship once. Several source blocks may illustrate the\nsame invariant; ground one precise actor/condition/mechanism explanation in all of\nthose IDs instead of narrating each fragment or each balance/table cell in turn.\nThat shared explanation must teach the actual contribution, not a generic claim\nthat a figure exists. Retain a new exception, assumption, branch or different\nmechanism explicitly. Repeated numerical substitutions, table snapshots, and\ninverse cases need only their shared rule plus the meaningful contrast. Use a\nrepresentative printed value only when it helps explain a new point. Do not copy\nevery original value merely to prove that it was read.\nWhen a classification is the lesson, explain the relation and constituents in one\nconcept; give a constituent its own card only if it teaches an independently useful\nmechanism/condition, rather than another dictionary-like label. Avoid an umbrella\ncard which repeats those cards. Definitions state the meaning, explanations add\nthe reasoning; do not repeat the same sentence across them.\nKeep main teaching self-contained. Optional easyExplanation must add a specific\nnew intermediate link or representation; if the main explanation already supplies\nthat link, omit the optional segment instead of a shorter paraphrase. Never remove\nan essential condition or formula from the main teaching. There is no hard text\nlength limit; use the length needed for the distinct learning points, not the\nnumber of source fragments. Source ownership and exact technical checks still run.\n'

METHOD_SELECTION_RULES = '\nEXAMPLE SELECTION AND TECHNICAL SAFETY\nDo not solve practice questions merely because their printed answer is visible.\nTeach a new method, its conditions, essential setup and the key reasoning step;\nretain a worked example only when the general explanation would otherwise leave\nthat particular step unclear. A long routine algebraic continuation after that\nstep can be omitted with the existing exact-source exercise disposition. Do not\nmake a blank generic coverage claim: retain every new rule/condition in main,\nand use the supported exerciseSelection/sourceDisposition for omitted practice.\nThis is a selection decision within the current request, not an extra call.\nNever compress a chain into a false identity. If an optional worked chain is\nretained, substitution signs, root/domain branches, coefficient bounds and array\nbranch behavior must still be consistent between adjacent steps. An optional\neasy paragraph cannot supply a missing condition of the main explanation.\n'

